a("### 8.6 E7: Cross-sample validation (two independent groups of women from the same study)\n")
a("Math note: `docs/math/E7_cross_sample.md`. **Terminology: this is cross-sample validation, not cross-dataset validation.** The 95 single-session women and the 65 longitudinal women are disjoint groups of women, but they come from the same study (presumably the same laboratory, assays and recruitment period; the files say nothing to the contrary). A second, truly independent dataset has not been used (see `docs/cross_dataset_candidates.md`). **Primary setting:** all standardisation and transformation statistics, and all hyper-parameters (inner cross-validation grouped by woman), come from the training group only; the baseline is the training-group mean. Models: baseline, ridge (scikit-learn), ridge from scratch, random forest, gradient boosting; feature sets A, B, C, D, D2; three targets.\n")
sz = df(E7["sizes"]); claim(int(sz.women_in_both.max()) == 0, "no woman in both train and test")
a("| Direction | Training rows / women | Test rows / women | Women in both |\n|---|---|---|---|")
for d_ in DIRN: a(f"| {DIRN[d_]} | {val(E7['sizes'], dict(direction=d_), 'train_rows', '{:.0f}', label=f'E7 train rows {d_}')} / {val(E7['sizes'], dict(direction=d_), 'train_women', '{:.0f}', label=f'E7 train women {d_}')} | {val(E7['sizes'], dict(direction=d_), 'test_rows', '{:.0f}', label=f'E7 test rows {d_}')} / {val(E7['sizes'], dict(direction=d_), 'test_women', '{:.0f}', label=f'E7 test women {d_}')} | {val(E7['sizes'], dict(direction=d_), 'women_in_both', '{:.0f}', label=f'E7 women in both {d_}')} |")
