a(f"\n**Answer.** In neither direction do hormones improve prediction beyond phase once the multiple comparisons are accounted for: the smallest adjusted one-sided p-value for an improvement over all {calc('E7 number of hormone tests', int(len(HT)), '{:.0f}', E7['hormone_tests'], 'rows')} comparisons is {calc('E7 min Holm improve all', float(HT.p_holm_all_improve.min()), '{:.3f}', E7['hormone_tests'], 'min p_holm_all_improve')} (Holm) and {calc('E7 min FDR improve all', float(HT.p_fdr_all_improve.min()), '{:.3f}', E7['hormone_tests'], 'min p_fdr_all_improve')} (FDR). The single uncorrected hint of an improvement (one-sided raw p = {calc('E7 smallest raw one-sided p', float(mi.p_improve_one_sided), '{:.3f}', E7['hormone_tests'], 'min p_improve_one_sided')}, {mi.direction.replace('_', ' ')}, {TN[mi.target]}, {mi.model}) is a change in RMSE of {calc('E7 hint dRMSE', float(mi.delta_RMSE), '{:+.4f}', E7['hormone_tests'], 'delta_RMSE of that row')} on an outcome with a baseline RMSE of {val(E7['metrics'], dict(sample=mi.direction, target=mi.target, model='baseline', fset='-'), 'RMSE', '{:.3f}', label='E7 baseline RMSE of the hint row')}: practically nil. In direction 1 hormones make predictions *worse* in {agg(E7['hormone_tests'], Q1 + ' and ci_lo > 0', None, 'count', '{:.0f}', label='E7 dir1 C vs A worse')} of {agg(E7['hormone_tests'], Q1, None, 'count', '{:.0f}', label='E7 dir1 C vs A tests')} comparisons by the uncorrected interval (none survives the correction), in direction 2 there is no difference in either direction. Details and the second family (hormones alone versus the baseline): `results/ext_e7_hormone_tests.csv`.\n")
