a(f"\nFigure: `results/fig_e7_shift.png`. Of the {calc('E7 number of variables compared', int(len(SV)), '{:.0f}', E7['shift_variables'], 'rows')} variables, {calc('E7 variables with SMD CI excluding 0', nsig, '{:.0f}', E7['shift_variables'], 'smd_lo > 0 or smd_hi < 0')} have an SMD interval that excludes 0: " + "; ".join(f"{r.label} ({r.smd_long_minus_cross:+.2f})" for r in sigv.itertuples()) + f". The Kolmogorov-Smirnov tests on first sessions find no significant difference for any variable after the Holm correction (smallest adjusted p {calc('E7 min KS Holm', float(SV.ks_p_first_holm.min()), '{:.3f}', E7['shift_variables'], 'min ks_p_first_holm')}). All SMDs of the questionnaire scores and of the three targets are small and their intervals include 0.\n")
